                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Cute little puzzle game. Game starts out really easy and adds new mechanics every couple of levels. The first few levels will make you feel like you're playing a game for kids, while the final couple of levels (50 levels in total) are quite challenging and will require multiple tries. Due to the way new mechanics are added, the increase in difficulty feels quite natural and didn't make me feel bored. The new mechanics are introduced without hand holding or explanation, but they work intuitive so that wasn't a problem. Though I must admit that in the end the levels were so large, it was impossible to visualize a solution, so it ended up being more trial and error than actually trying to solve a puzzle. \n\nAll in all, definitely a game I can recommend for about 2 hours of casual brain training for a small price.",
